{"name":"St. Petersburg","hex":"#dee8f3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"St. Petersburg","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative form of Saint Petersburg: A federal city and federal subject of Russia, known between 1914 and 1924 as Petrograd and between 1924 and 1991 as Leningrad; the former capital of Russia, from 1713 to 1728 and 1732 to 1918.","A city in Pinellas County, Florida, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/St._Petersburg"}],"entries":[{"title":"Saint Petersburg","blocks":[{"text":"Saint Petersburg, formerly known as Petrograd (Петроград), and later Leningrad (Ленинград), is the second-largest city in Russia, after Moscow, the nation's capital. Situated on the Neva River at the head of the Gulf of Finland on the Baltic Sea, its area of 1,439 square kilometers (556 sq mi) makes it the smallest administrative division of Russia by area. The city had a population of 5,601,911 residents as of 2021, with more than 6.4 million people living in the metropolitan area. Saint Petersburg is the fourth-most populous city in Europe, the most populous city on the Baltic Sea, and the world's northernmost city of more than 1 million residents. As the former capital of the Russian Empire, and a historically strategic Baltic port, it is governed as a federal city."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Spb_06-2017_img20_StMichael_Castle_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Spb_06-2017_img20_StMichael_Castle_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Petersburg"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Winter_Palace_Panorama_3.jpg/500px-Winter_Palace_Panorama_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Winter_Palace_Panorama_3.jpg/1280px-Winter_Palace_Panorama_3.jp